WEBVTT

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.140
Before, Selectors for the 
battles were chosen randomly,

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.070
but now they're being chosen 
from among former players.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.160
I don't know who's behind it, though.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.160
So both of you are Selectors already?

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.600
Now that we're Selectors, 
we can't escape the battles.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.770
Inevitability.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.920
That's what the Selector battles are.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.630
Yeah, I know.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.120
I've decided...

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.420
I'm going to win the battles and 
get Chi-chan's memories back.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:06.930
Concern.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.660
I was actually a little worried.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.570
You said you'd never do this again,

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.080
so I was worried you weren't 
in a good mental state.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.840
Yeah.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.370
I was really shocked.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.580
But I guess we didn't need to worry.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.640
Huh? Why?

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.670
If you're capable of baking us a new 
kind of cookie in this situation,

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.430
you probably aren't that concerned at all.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:29.210
Yes.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:33.500
Huh? Well, you both said 
you liked the last ones...

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.100
Delicious.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.530
Yes, they are good.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:37.680
Yeah, the cinnamon is perfect.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.760
I'm serious about this!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.550
So serious, I can't sleep at night.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.670
But you got up early to bake cookies.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.390
Riru!

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.130
Confirmation.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:50.310
How much of this situation 
were you able to predict?

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.650
I planned on being a Selector 
again, no matter what.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:58.410
But I didn't expect to be 
dragged into it like this.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.040
It was a complete surprise.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.400
So all Selectors in these 
battles are veterans?

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.120
Probably.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.790
The one I fought yesterday was a veteran 
from the first Selector battles.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.750
Is it possible that anyone who was ever 
a Selector will be forced to participate?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.480
I don't think so.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.230
Riru?

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.570
The number of participants right now

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:22.450
is far lower than the total 
number of previous Selectors.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.740
Yeah.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.800
The number might increase, but...

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.290
Doubt.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:32.170
Is it really possible for Suzuko-san 
to get back Chinatsu-san's memories?

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.900
Riru said there's a chance.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.300
To be honest, I'm not sure.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.680
All I can tell you is that the rules don't 
say the memories have to be yours.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.430
All LRIGs should have the battle 
rules imprinted in their minds,

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.890
but this time it's vague.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.330
It's like there's a lot that's being hidden...

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.240
Fundamental.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.040
First, I need to get back my LRIG.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:00.800
This is a key card I acquired.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.130
There's an LRIG, Milulun, inside.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.000
Try touching it.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.530
You can't just hand over an LRIG, then...

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.030
She become an LRIG?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.370
Yes... At the start, she didn't have an LRIG.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.100
So she used her key card,

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.750
and the Selector became an LRIG and 
participated in the battle directly.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.460
So that's how you use a key card.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:43.620
That means Selectors who were once LRIGs 
can unlock it to release their own powers.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.930
Wait, that means I can become 
an LRIG and fight if I have to!

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.320
With you, Hanayo-san, I can beat anyone!

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.430
Yeah.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.900
Okay, Hitoe.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.190
I'll get Midoriko back for you!

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.840
Yuzuki...

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.130
Be careful.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:06.360
That Layla girl seems really dangerous.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.640
I know.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.330
First, we'll look for her.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.420
We can start by—

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.980
Start by what?

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.330
R-Ruuko?

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.560
What were you talking about?

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.260
Wh-What were we...

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:21.020
There's this new cake place 
we wanted to try out.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.810
Right, Hitoe?

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:23.800
Y-Yeah!

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.790
A cake place? I want to go!

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:29.260
Uh... Oh, right! I've got work, so I can't go today.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.300
Let's go tomorrow.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.680
O-Okay...

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.830
Great!

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.680
Bye, Ruuko!

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.180
B-Bye...

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.180
I-I'm going to go home and do homework.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:41.450
Bye.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.650
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.610
If you lose, your LRIG is taken.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.370
That's the focal point of these battles, isn't it?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:50.830
Inevitable.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.580
The weight of each individual 
battle is much greater.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.350
Hanna-chan, what will you do now?

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:00.220
Idea. Even if you can't get one 
in exchange for nothing,

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.480
you may be able to get an 
LRIG if you pay a price.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:07.930
If I fight and deliberately lose...

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.260
Danger.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:12.260
If you do that, you'll lose a memory coin.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:18.520
I think we need to get more information 
before we decide if that's the best move.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:23.760
Fortunately, I have up to ninety days.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:24.760
Yeah.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:29.680
Whether we gather information 
or hand over coins and LRIGs,

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:33.740
it'll be more advantageous 
to act as a group this time.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.830
So that means we have an advantage!

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.520
Huh? We <i>are</i> working together, right?

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:41.400
Yes.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.710
Correct.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:45.670
Oh, dear.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.880
I'm out of eggs.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.730
Grandma, I'll go get some!

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:51.840
Will you?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.840
I'll let you do that for me, then.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:54.930
Sure!

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.420
Eggs, eggs, eggs!

00:06:58.420 --> 00:06:59.460
Meow!

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.740
Eggs, eggs...

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.270
<i>Shiro...</i>

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:13.970
<i>Shiro...</i>

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:14.850
Who's there?

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.470
Who's there?

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:20.550
<i>Shiro, come here.</i>

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.020
<i>Shiro...</i>

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:23.660
<i>Shiro.</i>

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.670
What? I don't like this...

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.880
<i>Come here.</i>

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.520
<i>Come here, Shiro.</i>

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.360
Tama?

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.510
What's wrong?

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:38.070
Ruu...

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:43.040
Ruu, I heard a weird voice!

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.830
I'm scared, Ruu!

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.520
What kind of voice?

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.560
I don't know...

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:59.870
It's okay. Nobody's here.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.100
Really?

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.630
Welcome home, Ruu.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.900
Thanks. Running an errand?

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.710
Yeah. I'm going to buy eggs.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.850
Let's go get them together, then.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:13.050
Okay!

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.220
<i>A Selector battle between a 
small number of participants...</i>

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.360
<i>Winners and losers are almost entirely 
decided after a single battle.</i>

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.940
<i>It's almost as if...</i>

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.570
This might be a little fun, actually.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.180
Fun? The Selector battles?

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.530
No, I mean, of course I'm scared.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.550
But it's like...

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:40.720
Last time, I was so worried and alone,

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:44.500
but now I can fight with you 
and Kiyoi-chan at my side.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.080
Question.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.710
Do you really intend to restore 
Chinatsu-san's memories?

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.700
Yes, why?

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:53.700
Concern.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:57.220
I'm well aware of the risks involved 
in getting memories back.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.560
In the previous battles,

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.290
Chinatsu-san set up Selector 
battles under Satomi's direction.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.920
Her actions brought sorrow to many Selectors

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.770
and destroyed the personality 
of her friend, Shirai-san.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.350
When she gets her memories back,

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:14.990
will she be able to forgive herself?

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:21.120
Can you still tell me that 
she should get them back?

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:23.060
I...

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.190
Concern.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.960
There's something else bothering me.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:31.850
Isn't there a chance that Chinatsu-san 
will be chosen for these battles, as well?

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.170
Suzuko.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:35.860
Riru?

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:38.090
A new Selector was just born.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:44.230
We meet again, Chi-chan.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.600
Who are you?

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.480
Meru.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:49.810
Meru?

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.770
The same name...

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.470
You gave it to me.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.480
You don't remember, do you?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.540
That's okay, though.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.240
It's all in here.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.040
After the last battles, I disappeared.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.710
But I was brought back,

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:10.580
along with your memories.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.210
They didn't disappear!

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.240
Even my memories with Suzu?

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:19.260
Win enough battles, and you 
can get them all back.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.540
Get them back...

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.730
Welcome to the Selector 
battles, Morikawa Chinatsu.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.380
Satomi Kou's favorite.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.830
Should I bring her to my side, or...

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:40.700
<i>Suzu?</i>

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:42.710
Chi-chan! Where are you?

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:45.140
<i>I've become a Selector.</i>

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:46.410
Chi...

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:49.170
It was just like you told me.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:52.860
If I win the battles, she said, 
I can get all my memories back.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.030
Amazing, isn't it?

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:56.360
I can remember everything I forgot.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:59.880
<i>Don't, Chi-chan! You don't remember 
anything about the battles, do you?</i>

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:02.880
I'll be fine. Meru is with me.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:04.660
<i>But it's dangerous!</i>

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:08.810
Soon, you won't have to look sad anymore.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.850
<i>I want to laugh and share the 
memories we treasured. Don't you?</i>

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:16.860
Chi-chan, listen.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.470
I'll get your memories back!

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.320
So don't do the battles...

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.510
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:25.580
<i>But this is my problem.</i>

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:32.280
Sudden development.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.600
This is dangerous.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.500
If Chinatsu-san runs into Carnival...

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.000
We have to stop her.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.530
Riru, do you know where Chi-chan is?

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:44.390
I can approximate a Selector's direction, 
but I don't know if it's Chinatsu...

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:45.450
Tell me.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.230
For now, head toward the station.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:48.130
Emergency.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:50.300
Let's have Kiyoi-san help us, too.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.390
Okay. I'll look.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.470
Piruluk.

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:56.020
Right.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.900
Riru, which way do I go?

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.480
Riru?

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.370
What's going on?

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:11.660
Piruluk...

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.290
Selectors are gathering in this town.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:18.960
Lying to a friend really hurts...

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.260
Yeah, but we can't help it.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.320
We can't tell Ruuko.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.220
Yeah.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:28.560
Hanayo-san, we made it to 
the town we were going for.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.600
Which way now?

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.400
Hanayo-san, what's wrong?

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.080
Are there no Selectors here?

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:34.850
The opposite.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:37.240
There are Selectors everywhere.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.990
Morikawa Chinatsu?

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:56.880
You're...

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.240
Sorry. I'm in a hurry.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.300
Wait.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.510
Did something happen?

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.180
I just saw Morikawa Chinatsu over there...

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:12.530
She became a Selector?

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.100
Yes.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.100
No way... Why?

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.580
But the Selector battles have already begun.

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:20.920
Damn it!

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:24.430
How am I supposed to get my 
LRIG back if I can't fight?

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.080
That bitch Piruluk...

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.160
That girl is a Selector?

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.910
Yes, I'm sure of it.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.300
Selector...

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.430
You're a Selector?

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.040
Good, I've been looking for one!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.070
Lucky Aki!

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:41.280
Aki-lucky!

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.380
Let's battle, okay?

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.340
Huh? She has no LRIG...

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.440
We can't fight, then.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:49.880
Let's go, Chi-chan.

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:50.430
Yeah.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.760
Hey.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.000
Hell no.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.400
I've finally found a Selector. 
I'm not letting you go.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.400
Fight me! All right?

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:00.900
Why is this happening to me?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.730
Am I just supposed to disappear?!

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.360
Please! I'm going to disappear!

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.280
I don't want to disappear!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:13.370
If you want, I can introduce 
you to the bookmaker...

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:16.910
Wait! Hey!

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:19.440
Suzuko..

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:23.380
Two Selectors. On the other side of that building.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:29.490
Two... On the other side of the building?

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:30.720
Yeah.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:31.770
Caution.

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:34.540
If these are different Selectors, 
we might end up in a battle.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.680
Yeah, but if it's Chi-chan...

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:39.720
Kiyoi-san?

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:40.480
Yes?

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.200
Yes.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.480
Acknowledgment.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.800
She saw Chinatsu-san.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.010
Let's go!

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.840
They're heading in the other direction.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.220
Who was that?

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.650
Another one, from a different direction.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:01.880
You finally came!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.590
I got sick of waiting.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.910
Layla-san...

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:06.860
This is her?!

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.070
You're Kurebayashi Yuzuki?

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:11.720
H-How do you know who I am?

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:15.230
Someone was nice enough to 
tell me all kinds of things.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.310
More importantly...

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.340
You've come to do it, haven't you?

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:20.390
With me!

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:21.600
Midoriko!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.060
Hitoe...

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.800
Your name's Midoriko, huh?

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.890
Come on, hurry.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:29.880
Yuzuki...

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:30.610
Don't worry.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.630
I'll win and get Midoriko back.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:34.450
Hanayo-san.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:35.410
Yeah.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:38.500
Open!

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:56.060
Yuzuki, an LRIG has to do 
what their Selector says.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:58.310
Don't hold back. Attack with all your strength.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:15:59.520
Right!

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:04.310
Unlock. Coin bet.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:09.880
Out of the way.

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:12.560
Turn end.

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:13.570
Now, come on.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:16.750
I didn't expect her to take over in turn one.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.220
Hanayo-san, grow!

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.730
Summon two Flathro.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.700
Use their effects to add SIGNI to my hand.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.040
Attack!

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.960
Wimpy.

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:36.090
Wimpy! Wimpy! Wimpy!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.680
Hanayo-san!

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.020
Hey, you.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:46.860
If you don't use your trump 
card soon, I'll crush her.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.310
Unlock! Coin bet!

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:04.330
I'll help you.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.880
Let's give it all we've got.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:07.920
Right.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.320
Summon Sergeant and Captain!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:13.970
ARTS: Thunderclap of Violent Supremacy!

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.620
This is great.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:33.440
This is how a battle should be.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:34.440
Coin bet!

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:35.900
Doping!

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.790
F1, Road, Ride Attack!

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.810
The goal of the battle is different?

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:47.700
Analysis.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:48.960
That's the only possible conclusion.

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:51.820
A minimal number of players and harsh rules.

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.180
The losing players are quickly 
removed from the game,

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:57.430
destroying even the rule involving 
losing and winning coins.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:58.890
This battle is like...

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.850
Like?

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:04.310
A battle to decide only one winner.

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:06.250
Only one?

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:15.430
Yuzuki...

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:16.650
Hanayo-san!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.740
Well, that's how it goes.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.200
Why?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.210
I thought you left the battle 
once you got five coins.

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.240
Leave the battle?

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:26.200
No way!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.340
I haven't had enough yet.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:29.330
Bring them.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:32.790
You have strong friends, right?

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.170
Yuzuki...

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:49.770
Chi-chan!

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:54.440
Hey, do you remember this face?

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:57.530
You and I were partners.

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:02.320
If you want to be stimulated, 
like you were back then...

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:05.300
I'll give you that stimulation, 
Morikawa Chinatsu.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.290
Stimulation...

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.500
Don't be fooled.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.600
Meru?

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:11.200
He wasn't your partner.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.600
He was just using you!

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.310
It's your choice.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:17.460
Join me or...

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.220
disappear here.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:30.840
There she is!

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.680
Well, that's interesting.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.900
The LRIG who traded places 
with the hot boy, and...

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:41.480
Stay away from him!

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:42.760
Who are you?

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:45.020
Don't worry about me.

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.500
Just don't do anything dangerous.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:48.600
This is my chance.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.160
If I can get my memories back, then I...

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.790
Morikawa-san, you should be 
careful about your battles.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.700
You know me, too?

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.510
I don't know you people.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:00.880
I don't know you...

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:02.200
I don't know this place...

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.220
Or even how important they were to me.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:08.710
I want it all back!

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.900
Suzuko-san asked me to stop you.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.030
Suzu did?

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.300
That's right.

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:17.190
She's a dear friend to you, right?

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.990
Don't do anything crazy!

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:21.530
If something happened to 
you, Shou-chan would...

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.660
Shou-chan?

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:27.740
<i>Morikawa?</i>

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:30.870
Chi-chan!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.080
Hey!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.530
So what's left of her 
memories reacted to that?

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:36.080
I won't let you touch her.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:37.470
Oh?

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.220
Kiyoi...

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:40.720
It has to happen sometime.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.510
Can you beat him?

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.860
I couldn't last time.

00:20:44.860 --> 00:20:46.010
But I can't lose.

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:49.680
I'll make it plain for you, little bitch.

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:51.880
You're not the queen.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:54.310
You're a pawn, and it's time 
for you to leave the board.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.440
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.070
<i>Do I...</i>

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:03.190
<i>Do I have to just watch?</i>

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.620
Why?

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:11.950
Wish...

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:14.370
Wish...

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:16.180
Tell us your wish...

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:16.730
Who's there?

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:19.240
Your wish.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.060
What do you want to do?

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:23.360
My wish...

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:28.890
My wish is... I want to save her!

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:31.320
In Shou-chan's place!

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:36.350
What is this?

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:40.320
I'll be joining the battle, too!

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:48.160
You'd better entertain me, at least a little.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.320
Open.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:56.000
Gathering / Vortex and Turbid Water

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.100
I was doing the Selector battles...

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:29.360
Hello!

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:30.880
I'm special!

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.430
Wasn't the door supposed to open?

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:34.380
You know how to use the key card, right?

00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:35.330
It's to win.

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:36.430
Let's do it again, okay?

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:38.280
That's WIXOSS.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:41.020
Determination / Warmth and Pain

00:23:38.280 --> 00:23:41.020
Determination / Warmth and Pain.
